args: opentide new --help
exit: 0

━━━ stdout
Scaffold a threat, objective or rule from its template

The new file gets a fresh UUID, today's date, your git author and the catalogue's organisation, and is named the way opentide lint expects. Required values nobody has chosen yet are placeholders, listed in the output: replace them, then run opentide validate --file on the path.

␛[1m␛[4mUsage:␛[0m ␛[1mopentide new␛[0m <COMMAND>

␛[1m␛[4mCommands:␛[0m
  ␛[1mthreat␛[0m     Scaffold a threat
  ␛[1mobjective␛[0m  Scaffold a detection objective
  ␛[1mrule␛[0m       Scaffold a detection rule

␛[1m␛[4mOptions:␛[0m
      ␛[1m--help␛[0m
          Print help

Examples:
  $ opentide new threat --name "Credential Dumping"

━━━ stderr · empty
